Comments:
    Tests the following:
    - experimental/timestep_sts_2
    - initial_condition/blob
    
    The setup models a negative entropy perturbation falling in an adiabatically
    stratified background. The system has nu and K constant.
    
    With the parameters of this sample (i.e. when the diffusive constraint on
    the timestep is dominant), performance is comparable to timestep_sts.
    
    If we change to nu=8e-3,hcond0=8e-2,Fbot=-8e-2, timestep_sts crashes after
    75 iterations, while timestep_sts_2 does not; the performance of the latter
    is comparable to that of the default RK3 timestepper.
    
    Note that just like in timestep_sts, the dt diagnostic has the wrong value
    (see the comment in src/experimental/timestep_sts_2.f90:134).
